menu "SET sensor bus (BMP388 + LSM6DSOX)"

    choice SET_SENSOR_BUS
        prompt "Interface"
        default SET_SENSOR_BUS_I2C
        help
            Both sensors share the same three wires (GPIO54, GPIO19, GPIO18),
            so they run as one bus or the other -- never a mix.

            SPI IS NOT IMPLEMENTED YET. Selecting it builds, but every
            transfer returns ESP_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED and no sensor comes up.
            I2C is the default until the SPI branch of sensor_bus.c is
            filled in.

            AFTER CHANGING THIS, REMOVE ALL POWER (battery and USB) before
            testing. The BMP388 switches itself to SPI the first time its CS
            pin goes low and stays in SPI until it loses power. Pressing reset
            on the ESP32 does not cut power to the sensors.

        config SET_SENSOR_BUS_SPI
            bool "SPI (NOT IMPLEMENTED -- stubs only)"

        config SET_SENSOR_BUS_I2C
            bool "I2C (working)"
    endchoice

    config SET_SENSOR_SPI_FREQ_HZ
        int "SPI clock (Hz)"
        depends on SET_SENSOR_BUS_SPI
        range 100000 10000000
        default 1000000
        help
            Kept so the SPI branch has a clock to use once it is written.
            Both sensors allow up to 10 MHz. 1 MHz moves a full IMU sample in
            about 0.1 ms and is far more forgiving of long wires and breakout
            level-shifters. Raise it only after the chip-ID check passes.

    config SET_SENSOR_I2C_FREQ_HZ
        int "I2C clock (Hz)"
        depends on SET_SENSOR_BUS_I2C
        range 100000 400000
        default 400000
        help
            400 kHz is the fastest standard I2C speed both sensors support.
            Drop to 100000 if the bus scan at boot finds nothing.

endmenu
